  "notes": "REGISTER:\nPolite/formal (お + {詫|わ}び). The お- prefix makes it more polite.\n\nUSAGE:\n- お{詫|わ}び{申|もう}し{上|あ}げます (I humbly apologize - very formal)\n- お{詫|わ}びいたします (I apologize - formal)\n- お{詫|わ}びの{言葉|ことば} (words of apology)\n- お{詫|わ}びの{品|しな}/{印|しるし} (gift of apology)\n\nIN BUSINESS:\n- お{詫|わ}び{状|じょう} (letter of apology)\n- お{詫|わ}び{文|ぶん} (apology statement)\n- お{詫|わ}びとお{知|し}らせ (apology and notice)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- お{詫|わ}び (formal apology)\n- {謝罪|しゃざい} (apology - more formal, often public)\n- ごめんなさい (sorry - casual)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {詫|わ}びる (to apologize - verb)\n- {謝|あやま}る (to apologize)\n- {陳謝|ちんしゃ} (formal apology)",
